Generated Surge modules, except YouTube_remove_ads.sgmodule and StartUpAds.sgmodule, are adaptations of
Loon configuration templates from https://hub.kelee.one/ and retain the
supplied author metadata and source URL. They are distributed for
non-commercial use under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/

YouTube_remove_ads.sgmodule and its mirrored scripts come from Maasea's
Apache-2.0-licensed native Surge module. SelfSurge adds category metadata and
replaces its script URLs with local mirrors. The upstream license is mirrored
at resources/licenses/Maasea-sgmodule-LICENSE.

StartUpAds.sgmodule is adapted from ddgksf2013's Quantumult X rewrite at
https://ddgksf2013.top/rewrite/StartUpAds.conf (fetched with User-Agent: surge).
It retains upstream attribution and supplements the existing modules, which
take precedence for duplicate patterns and app hosts. Non-ad routing and
TestFlight/membership tweaks are excluded. Upstream terms remain applicable;
SelfSurge does not relicense this source.

Files under scripts/ and resources/ are unmodified mirrors. Copyright and
license terms remain with their respective upstream authors. sources.json
records each upstream URL and SHA-256 checksum; SelfSurge does not relicense
those files.

Script-Hub was studied as a behavioral reference. Its GPL-3.0 source code was
not copied into SelfSurge.
